WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.900
This morning,

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.568
the US has

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.903
no embassy operating in Sudan, a country

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.805
on the brink of civil war.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.873
President Biden announcing

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.274
that US diplomatic personnel

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.376
and their families

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.444
have been evacuated from Sudan.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:12.545
Secretary of State

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.514
Antony Blinken adding that operations

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:14.981
at the US

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.016
Embassy in Khartoum

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.585
have been temporarily suspended.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:19.753
CNN's

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.921
Sam Kiley is reporting on the situation

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.056
from Djibouti for us.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.358
And Sam, how was the extraction of U.S.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.626
personnel carried out?

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:27.260
And our officials

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.363
saying why it was necessary

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.066
Well, let's start with why

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.200
it was necessary

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.702
that, Christine, you say that

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.303
Sudan is on the brink of civil war.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.571
I think from the American

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.173
and International perspective.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.042
It is a country in the throes

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.711
of a very violent, actual civil war.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.546
There are, for example,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.916
Sudanese jets bombarding positions inside

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.384
their own capital.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.053
And it's that level of violence

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:53.586
that provoked

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.255
not just the United States,

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:55.555
but an

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:58.191
enormous international military effort

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.327
centered here in Djibouti or out of here

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:02.862
in Djibouti, mainly

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.799
to try to get international aid workers

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.100
and other people, students

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.501
and all kinds of internationals

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.502
out of that country.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.438
Now, when it comes to the United States.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.739
They were in the vanguard

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.375
of the evacuation operations

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.709
that began over the weekend

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.511
with a very daring raid

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.514
effectively by some 100 Americans, mostly

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.217
special forces involving three Chinook

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.853
helicopters that took off from here

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.821
in Djibouti,

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.522
flew via Ethiopia,

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.157
where they refueled in Addis Ababa

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.660
and then flew very low and slow.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.028
They're not that fast.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:37.163
Aircraft at about 100 miles an hour

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.265
all the way to the Sudanese capital

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.701
itself, the scene of violence

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.769
where a cease fire

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.037
around the idea for their

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:45.939
celebrations for

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:46.473
the end of

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.374
Ramadan were not being observed in

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.843
any serious way.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.077
They were able to pluck out

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:53.379
just under 100 people, mostly

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:54.948
embassy staffers

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:55.849
plus their families

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.916
and a few internationals

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.551
who were co-located with them

00:01:58.551 --> 00:01:59.853
and take them out of out

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.221
to safety initially.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.322
In Ethiopia,

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.256
on the back of that,

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:03.590
an hour

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.591
or two later, British

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.693
special forces were on the ground.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.528
They had anticipated or planned

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:09.996
for the worst eventuality,

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.564
which was having to fight

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.633
and protect British citizens and others,

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.834
that they didn't have to do that.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.003
But they did have to do an 18 mile

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:20.340
30 kilometer road move to a desert

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.342
airstrip where they were able

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:24.477
to evacuate people alongside the French,

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:25.945
who were also engaged,

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.581
reportedly in some kind of brief clash,

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.216
or at least that is reported

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.085
to have been minor injuries,

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.153
perhaps on one person

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.554
being evacuated there.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:35.822
Now the international effort

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.290
is getting underway

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.658
there is extreme

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.827
violence continuing in Khartoum, the

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.328
the central prison there.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.563
That includes large number of

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.799
senior members of previous administration

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.268
have been let out

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:49.135
real concerns

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.203
that the place is collapsing

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.504
into violent anarchy

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.706
and more evacuations would be necessary.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:54.140
A battle

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.441
for power in Sudan

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.576
at the heart of the conflict

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.244
are these two men

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.646
that are up on your screen

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.246
right there,

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.814
Sudan's military leader, Abdel

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.650
Fattah Al-burhan,

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.585
and the commander of the paramilitary

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:06.553
rapid support

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:10.256
forces are Asaf Mohammed Hamdan, Dagalo.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:13.059
Now, until recently, they were allies.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.260
They worked together

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.895
to topple Sudan's former dictator.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:16.829
President Omar

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.165
al-Bashir in 2019

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.767
and played a crucial role

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:21.501
in orchestrating

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.270
the country's military coup in 2021.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.072
But tensions arose over

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.540
how to integrate the RCF

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.175
into the country's military

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.276
as part of plans

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.011
to restore civilian rule.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.646
So the key question here is

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.449
who would be subordinate to whom

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.051
under this new hierarchy will.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.186
Sources tell CNN that these hostilities

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.054
are the culmination

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:41.421
of what

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.488
both parties view

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.958
as an existential fight for dominance.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.259
So that is how we got here.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.026
So joining us now,

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:48.328
the White House is National

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:51.130
Security Council spokesperson spokesman

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:51.864
and that is Mr.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:52.398
John Kirby.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.033
John, thank you so much for joining us.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:54.901
I appreciate it.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.102
So you heard Sam Kiley

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.003
there on the ground.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.171
The US was able

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.206
to successfully get diplomats out

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:02.075
calling it fast and clean.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.143
Why not do the same sort of operation

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:04.877
with citizens?

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:05.945
Can the US carry out

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.113
a large scale operation

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.881
like that for citizens?

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.048
Well,

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:09.816
we have military

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.251
forces still pre-positioned

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.019
nearby in the region, Don,

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:13.620
if they're needed.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.354
But quite frankly,

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.389
the situation is not conducive

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.291
and not safe to try to conduct

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.525
some kind of a larger

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.661
military evacuation of American citizens.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:22.762
You saw from yourself,

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.230
from Sam's reporting,

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.932
actually the violence is increasing

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.033
is more dangerous today

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.468
than it was just yesterday,

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.569
the day before.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.570
And so the best advice

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.804
we can give to those Americans

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.539
who did not abide by our warnings

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:33.940
to leave

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.075
Sudan and not to travel to Sudan

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.777
is to stay sheltered in place,

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:38.611
stay safe

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.345
and secure

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.847
and off the streets of Khartoum.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.782
We are doing what we can

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.917
to help guide people who can move out

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:45.918
to get out

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:48.454
to potentially like land convoys

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:48.988
that are moving.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:49.255
In fact,

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.523
there are several dozen Americans

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:53.326
that we know of that are in a U.N.

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.394
led convoy

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.529
that's making its way to Port Sudan

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:57.563
over ground on.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:58.765
In fact, the U.S.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:04:59.899
military is flying

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:02.702
unmanned aerial assets over that convoy

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:03.970
so that we can maintain

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.571
some sort of situational awareness

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:06.939
in overwatch for them

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:07.840
to help protect them

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.275
as they make their way to Port Sudan.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.143
We're also

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.344
deploying naval assets

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:13.012
to Port Sudan in the Red Sea

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:13.880
in case Americans

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.114
to get out to Port Sudan

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.649
want to be be transported

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.251
elsewhere or need any kind of care.

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.686
All right. That's in case on their own.

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.721
But I just have to ask you, because,

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.156
you know, this vast and clean mission,

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:24.257
you're saying that it's dangerous.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.525
And we did hear it's dangerous

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:26.326
and Sam's reporting.

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:27.093
But Sudan's

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:27.827
military chief

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.562
said on Saturday morning,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:30.229
John,

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.397
that his troops would help

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:34.434
evacuate US diplomats and citizens.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.436
He said, and citizens.

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:37.470
But the US embassy said

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.871
that it was too dangerous.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:39.639
Do you think that there was

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.341
a missed opportunity

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:45.078
to get private citizens, US citizens out?

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:46.346
No, sir.

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:46.779
In fact,

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:47.947
we are doing everything

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.882
we can to help guide them.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:52.218
If there is a safe way to get out,

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:52.652
we're helping

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:54.053
guide them and give them information

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.121
we're in touch

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:57.123
with hundreds of American citizens

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:58.725
that are there who want

00:05:58.725 --> 00:05:59.892
who may want to leave.

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:00.460
It's up to them,

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.128
of course, to decide to do that.

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:02.729
We're doing the best

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:03.363
we can to give them

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:03.963
the information

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:04.564
that they need, that

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.933
they can rely on, and to do so safely.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:07.767
But honestly,

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:09.702
the fighting in Khartoum is not

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:10.503
in a situation

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:11.904
where we would want people

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.806
moving about to freely or to aggressively

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:14.140
right now.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.509
The safest thing for many Americans to do

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.377
who didn't get out

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:18.644
when they were warned to get out

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.413
is to stay safe right now.

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:20.780
And let's

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.181
see if the situation can improve

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.116
in the meantime, Don.

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.183
And I know I'm running on here,

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.651
but we are working closely

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:26.986
with both military factions

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:27.887
and these leaders.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:28.688
Now, General Hamidi,

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:29.722
General Beran,

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.290
to get them to put down their arms

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.525
and abide by a cease fire,

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:33.659
they both say they want

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.595
so that the conditions can be more safe.

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:35.895
Okay.

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:36.462
So you said

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.430
you were in touch with hundreds,

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.131
but there are

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:40.233
about 16,000 or so people

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:41.834
who have to get out of this country.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:42.735
Are you able to

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:43.803
you're not able to get in touch

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:45.037
with all of them? Right.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:45.638
Well, Don,

00:06:45.638 --> 00:06:46.873
I want to push back on this idea

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:48.408
that there are 16,000 Americans

00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:49.475
who want to get out.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:51.077
We don't have firm

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.412
estimates of the exact number

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:54.580
of Americans citizens who are in Sudan.

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:55.848
They don't have to register with us.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:56.582
They don't have to tell us

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:57.350
that they're there.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.752
We think the vast majority

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:01.354
of these are American citizens in Sudan

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:02.822
and they're not all in Khartoum.

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:03.823
Are dual nationals.

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:05.425
These are people who grew up in Sudan,

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:06.592
who have families, their work,

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:07.660
their businesses there,

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:08.995
who don't want to leave.

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:10.096
So I think we need to be careful

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.164
about that number.

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:12.999
There's a much smaller population

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:14.100
of American citizens

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.334
who don't work for the government

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:15.802
but work

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:17.069
who with partner agencies

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.204
like the American School

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:19.839
or Fulbright Scholar program

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:21.007
that we are in touch with.

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:21.974
And we're trying to get them

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.576
the best information we can to get out.

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:25.111
And as I said, several dozen,

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.979
we know today are in that U.N.

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.714
convoy heading to Port Sudan. Okay.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.750
So we talked about how dangerous it is.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.385
Is a US in contact

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:34.320
with either of these leaders

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.522
of these factions that are fighting?

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:37.089
Yes.

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.057
And there are efforts

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:39.525
and there are efforts by the US

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.461
to de-escalate or mediate.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:42.528
100%, Don,

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:43.396
we've been in touch with them

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:44.564
almost every day

00:07:44.564 --> 00:07:45.832
since the beginning of this crisis.

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:47.200
The fighting really started a week ago

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.067
Saturday.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:48.734
We've been in direct

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.436
touch with them at various levels, Don,

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:51.070
not just

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.405
not just at the State Department.

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:53.573
But even our senior military

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:54.640
leaders have been in touch with them

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.642
because these are two military men

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:57.910
to try to get them to, again,

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:58.978
abide by the cease fire

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.213
they both say they want.

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:01.147
What about the president

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:02.782
telling them to stop

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:04.283
We have been communicating

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:05.685
with both leaders again

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:06.919
at very various levels

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:08.488
and we'll continue to do that.

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.156
Is there anything that can be done

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:11.524
to target the leaders to get them

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:12.358
to stop the fighting

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:13.092
like sanctions,

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:15.461
targeting their wealth, etc.?

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:17.463
We have a lot of tools at our disposal

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:18.664
and we're sort of working our way

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:19.765
through that right now.

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:20.132
But again,

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.634
the focus is making sure

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:23.336
that we get the cease fire in place,

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:24.637
we get the violence to stop,

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:26.372
we get the tensions de-escalated

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:27.273
so that you can, again,

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:28.741
have those kinds of conversations

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:29.475
going forward.

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:30.743
I don't want to get ahead of decisions

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:31.711
we haven't made yet.

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:33.045
Our focus is really getting

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:33.980
the violence down

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:34.580
and helping

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.083
get those people who want to leave Sudan

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:38.751
to be able to do so safely

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:39.719
and provide them

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:40.486
the best options and

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:41.420
information to do that.

